WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.219
The same idea at other providers.

2
00:00:02.499 --> 00:00:06.104
Every major API now offers schema-constrained output.

3
00:00:06.384 --> 00:00:14.085
The names differ, and so do the subsets of JSON Schema they enforce, so read each provider’s limits before you port a schema.

4
00:00:14.365 --> 00:00:16.712
OpenAI calls it Structured Outputs.

5
00:00:16.992 --> 00:00:25.397
In the Responses API you set a text format of type json_schema with strict: true; the Python SDK’s responses.

6
00:00:25.677 --> 00:00:29.517
parse() accepts a Pydantic model and returns output_parsed.

7
00:00:29.797 --> 00:00:37.157
OpenAI distinguishes it from the older JSON mode, which guarantees valid JSON but not adherence to your schema.

8
00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:41.640
Refusals arrive as a separate content item you check before parsing.

9
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:50.005
Google’s Gemini API takes a JSON Schema with an application/json MIME type; the Python examples pass Model.

10
00:00:50.285 --> 00:00:54.531
model_json_schema() and validate with model_validate_json().

11
00:00:54.811 --> 00:01:04.965
The docs say some keywords, such as minLength and maxLength, are ignored rather than enforced, and they warn about schema-compliant but semantically incorrect outputs.

12
00:01:05.245 --> 00:01:18.472
xAI’s Grok API accepts a json_schema response format and Pydantic models, states that output is guaranteed to match when you use supported features, and lists other features as best effort.

13
00:01:18.752 --> 00:01:22.272
Open models get the same capability from the serving layer.

14
00:01:22.552 --> 00:01:34.136
vLLM, a widely used open-source inference server, supports JSON Schema, regex, fixed choices, and context-free grammars through backends such as xgrammar and guidance.

15
00:01:34.416 --> 00:01:39.920
Libraries such as Outlines (from the Willard and Louf paper) do the same in your own process.

16
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:48.520
This is a real advantage of open models: you control the grammar engine and can constrain to formats a hosted API doesn’t offer.
